<title>USA: Valspar proposes two-for-one stock split.</title>
<headline>Valspar proposes two-for-one stock split.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Valspar Corp said Wednesday it proposed a two-for-one stock split, which is contingent upon shareholder approval of an increase in its authorized shares to 120 million from 30 million.</p>
<p>The increase will be voted on at its February 26 annual meeting. After the stock split there would be about 43.8 million common shares outstanding.</p>
<p>Valspar is a coatings company.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
